  "text": " \n \n\n [2611.03577] Sonar-MoE: In-Backward Expert Updates for Memory-Efficient Mixture-of-Experts Training \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n Skip to main content \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Search \n \n \n \n \n \n Submit \n Donate \n \n Log in \n \n \n \n \n Search arXiv \n \n \n \n \n \n Press Enter to search &middot; Advanced search \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n--> \n\n \n \n Computer Science > Machine Learning \n \n\n \n arXiv:2611.03577 (cs)\n \n \n \n \n \n [Submitted on 2 Nov 2026] \n Title: Sonar-MoE: In-Backward Expert Updates for Memory-Efficient Mixture-of-Experts Training \n Authors: Avni Mittal , Avinash Anand , Ashutosh Kumar , Dikshant Kukreja , Kritarth Prasad , Chaitanya Lakhchaura , Rishitej Reddy Vyalla , Erik Cambria , Zhengkui Wang , Rajiv Ratn Shah View a PDF of the paper titled Sonar-MoE: In-Backward Expert Updates for Memory-Efficient Mixture-of-Experts Training, by Avni Mittal and 9 other authors \n View PDF \n HTML (experimental) \n\n\n\n \n Abstract: Most parameters of a Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) model belong to its experts, and standard training keeps every expert gradient in GPU memory until the optimizer step. This memory grows with the number and size of the experts, so it rises as MoE models scale. We introduce Sonar-MoE, which updates each expert tensor during the backward pass and frees its gradient right away. It brings optimizer-in-backward from dense models to batched MoE expert tensors, so the GPU never holds more than one layer of expert gradients. When we fine-tune OLMoE-1B-7B and Granite-3.1-3B-A800M in bf16 with two expert-kernel backends, Sonar-MoE lowers peak memory by 19% to 22%. Its updates are bitwise identical to standard training without expert gradient clipping, and held-out loss stays within 0.003 of all baselines. Each step also takes 17% to 23% less time than standard training with global-norm clipping. Updating whole batched tensors rather than individual experts is what keeps Sonar-MoE fast, as it avoids a 20% to 72% slowdown while using the same memory. Sonar-MoE matches optimizer-in-backward over all parameters in memory and speed while still clipping the dense parameters.\n \n\n \n \n \n Subjects: \n \n Machine Learning (cs.LG) ; Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI); Computation and Language (cs.CL); Performance (cs.PF) \n \n Cite as: \n arXiv:2611.03577 [cs.LG] \n \n \n \n (or \n arXiv:2611.03577v1 [cs.LG] for this version)\n \n \n \n \n https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2611.03577 \n \n \n Focus to learn more \n \n \n \n arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite (pending registration) \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Submission history From: Avni Mittal [ view email ] [v1] \n Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:30:00 UTC (299 KB) \n \n \n \n \n \n Full-text links: \n Access Paper: \n \n \nView a PDF of the paper titled Sonar-MoE: In-Backward Expert Updates for Memory-Efficient Mixture-of-Experts Training, by Avni Mittal and 9 other authors View PDF HTML (experimental) TeX Source\n \n \n \n view license \n \n \n \n Additional Features \n \n Audio Summary \n \n \n \n Current browse context: \n cs.LG \n\n \n \n < prev \n \n | \n next > \n \n \n new \n | \n recent \n | 2026-11 \n \n Change to browse by:\n \n cs \n cs.AI \n cs.CL \n cs.PF \n \n \n\n \n \n References & Citations \n \n SciX Google Scholar \n Semantic Scholar \n \n \n \n\n \n export BibTeX citation \n Loading... \n \n\n \n \n \n BibTeX formatted citation \n &times; \n \n \n loading... \n \n \n Data provided by: \n \n \n \n \n Bookmark \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Bibliographic Tools \n \n Bibliographic and Citation Tools \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Bibliographic Explorer Toggle \n \n \n \n Bibliographic Explorer ( What is the Explorer? ) \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Connected Papers Toggle \n \n \n \n Connected Papers ( What is Connected Papers? ) \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Litmaps Toggle \n \n \n \n Litmaps ( What is Litmaps? ) \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n scite.ai Toggle \n 