n as Hybrid Cloud Observability) Release Notes\n \n \n\n \n News & Announcements \n \n Evolving towards Observability\n \n \n Secure by Design\n \n \n Meet our Product Trainers\n \n THWACKcamp \n \n\n \n Connect with Us \n \n Technical Documentation\n \n \n Customer Portal\n \n \n Submit a Ticket\n \n \n THWACK Community\n \n \n Orange Matter Blog\n \n \n TechPod Episodes\n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n\n \n \n\n\n\n \n \n \r\n \r\n \r\n Documentation for Dameware DRS & MRC \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n Dameware 2026.3.1 release notes \r\n \r\n Formatting and layout changes \r\n Tracks formatting/layout/content changes to the release notes builder template \r\n \r\n \r\n Release date: November 3, 2026 \r\n \r\n \r\n Here's what's new in Dameware 2026.3.1. You can find the applicable system requirements here . \r\n Skipping a version? If you're upgrading from more than one version back, don't rely on this page alone &mdash; review the release notes aggregator to see everything that changed across the versions you&rsquo;re skipping , and across your SolarWinds Platform products . \r\n To view release notes, system requirements, and product guide (formerly known as administrator guide) PDFs for supported versions of Dameware, see Dameware previous versions . \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n New features and improvements in Dameware There were no features or improvements added for Dameware in this release. \r\n \r\n Fixed CVEs \r\n At SolarWinds, we prioritize the swift resolution of CVEs to ensure the security and integrity of our software. In this release, we have successfully addressed the following CVEs. \r\n \r\n SolarWinds CVEs \r\n SolarWinds would like to thank our Security Researchers below for reporting on the issue in a responsible manner and working with our security, product, and engineering teams to fix the vulnerability. \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n CVE-ID \r\n Vulnerability Title \r\n Description \r\n Severity \r\n Credit \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n CVE-2026-28327 \r\n SolarWinds Dameware DLL Hijacking Vulnerability \r\n SolarWinds Dameware was found to be affected by a DLL hijacking vulnerability. The hijack occurs during installations only and requires access to the local machine and admin privileges. \r\n 8.2 High \r\n Luiz Felipe Mol (Confu53) \r\n \r\n CVE-2026-28335 \r\n SolarWinds Dameware Buffer Overflow Vulnerability \r\n SolarWinds Dameware was found to be affected by a buffer overflow vulnerability that can result in remote code execution. Authentication is required. \r\n 8.4 High \r\n Greg Bernatowicz on the Boeing Enterprise Security Red Team \r\n \r\n CVE-2026-28336 \r\n SolarWinds Dameware Command Injection Vulnerability \r\n SolarWinds Dameware was found to be affected by a command injection vulnerability that could lead to the compromised of the remotely controlled host. Authentication is required. \r\n 9.9 Critical \r\n Greg Bernatowicz on the Boeing Enterprise Security Red Team \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n Third-party CVEs \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n CVE-ID \r\n Vulnerability title \r\n Description \r\n Severity \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n CVE-2026-111497 \r\n Brotli Decoder Buffer Overflow Vulnerability \r\n A buffer overflow vulnerability in the Brotli decoder (c/dec/decode.c) in Google Brotli versions 1.0.3 through 1.2.0 on all platforms allows a remote unauthenticated attacker to corrupt adjacent decoder state memory, disclose sensitive memory contents, cause a denial of service, or potentially execute arbitrary code using a crafted Brotli-compressed stream. Users need to update any Brotli libraries or binaries between 1.0.3 through 1.2.0 to the latest available version: 1.0.10 or 1.1.1 or 1.2.1. \r\n 9.8 Critical \r\n \r\n CVE-2026-40021 \r\n Improper Neutralization of Null Byte or NUL Character Vulnerability \r\n Apache Log4net's XmlLayout https://logging.apache.org/log4net/manual/configuration/layouts.html#layout-list and XmlLayoutSchemaLog4J https://logging.apache.org/log4net/manual/configuration/layouts.html#layout-list , in versions before 3.3.0, fail to sanitize characters forbidden by the XML 1.0 specification https://www.w3.org/TR/xml/#charsets in MDC property keys and values, as well as the identity field that may carry attacker-influenced data. This causes an exception during serialization and the silent loss of the affected log event. An attacker who can influence any of these fields can exploit this to suppress individual log records, impairing audit trails and detection of malicious activity. Users are advised to upgrade to Apache Log4net 3.3.0, which fixes this issue. \r\n 6.3 Medium \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n Installation or upgrade \r\n \r\n For information about installing Dameware, see the Dameware Installation Guides . \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n Dameware Remote Support (DRS) 12.2.4 and later versions feature security improvements to the saved hosts protection mechanism. As a result, you must back up your DRS registry settings and saved hosts from your previous Dameware version(s). See Back up Dameware Remote Support hosts on first launch after upgrade to versions 12.2.4 or later for additional information. \r\n \r\n \r\n Dameware Mini Remote Control (MRC) 12.2.2 and later versions feature security improvements to the saved hosts protection mechanism. As a result, you must back up your MRC registry settings and saved hosts from your previous Dameware version(s). See Back up Dameware Mini Remote Control settings and hosts during upgrade to version 12.2.2 or later for additional information. \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n To operate Dameware on Microsoft Windows 7, an administrator must follow the instructions in the following knowledge base article to install required security fixes: https://microsoft.com/en-us/download/details.aspx?id=47442 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n For information about upgrading Dameware, see Upgrade Dameware . \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n SolarWinds strongly recommends that upgrades be performed using the same admin account from the previous installation. \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n You may need to perform the Dameware upgrade using elevated privileges (as administrator). \r\n \r\n \r\n See the Limitations section in the Back up Dameware Remote Support hosts on first launch after upgrade to versions 12.2.4 or later for more details. \r\n \r\n \r\n See the Limitations section in the Back up Dameware Mini Remote Control settings and hosts during upgrade to version 12.2.2 or later for more details. \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n Customers should note that Microsoft SQL Server Compact Edition 4.0 SP1 can be removed from your computer only AFTER fully upgrading from Dameware Central Server 12.2.3 or an earlier version, and only if you are certain SQL Compact Edition is no longer required by any other program on the computer. \r\n Installer List \r\n \r\n Stand-alone installation \r\n The stand-alone installation requires each product to be individually activated on each computer. It is most useful for organizations with a small user base or with small or decentralized IT departments. These installers are available through your customer portal. \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n File name \r\n Description \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n SolarWinds-Dameware-MRC-64bit-St.exe \r\n Dameware Mini Remote Control (64-bit) Installer, used for stand-alone mode deployment \r\n \r\n \r\n SolarWinds-Dameware-MRC-32bit-St.exe \r\n Dameware Mini Remote Control (32-bit) Installer, used for stand-alone mode deployment \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n Centralized installation \r\n The centralized installation requires you to install and deploy at least the Dameware Central Server. License activation occurs on the server level, and users authenticate to the Central Server from any centralized Mini Remote Control installation. Centralized mode is useful for organizations with a large user base, with large or centralized IT departments, or with multiple Dameware product licenses managed from a single point. You must request these installers from your SolarWinds sales representative. \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n File name \r\n Description \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n SolarWinds-Dameware-MRC-64bit.exe \r\n Dameware Mini Remote Control (64-bit) Installer, used for centralized mode deployment \r\n \r\n \r\n SolarWinds-Dameware-MRC-32bit.exe \r\n Dameware Mini Remote Control (32-bit) Installer, used for centralized mode deployment \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n Stand-alone Licensing (MRC licenses) \r\n After installing the standard version of Dameware Mini Remote Control (DamewareMRC32-St.exe or DamewareMRC64-St.exe), you are prompted to enter the licensing information for your product. \r\n To evaluate the software, click Continue Evaluation. \r\n To license the software on a computer with Internet access: \r\n \r\n \r\n On the computer you want to license, click Start > All Programs > SolarWinds > Dameware Mini Remote Control > Enter Licensing Information. \r\n \r\n Select I have internet access and an activation key. \r\n Access the customer portal on the SolarWinds website at: https://www.solarwinds.com/customerportal . \r\n Log in using your SolarWinds customer ID and password. \r\n Click License Management. \r\n Navigate to your product, choose an activation key from the Unregistered Licenses section, and then copy the activation key. \r\n If you cannot find an activation key in the Unregistered Licenses section, contact SolarWinds Customer Support . \r\n Return to the Activate Mini Remote Control window, and then enter the activation key in the Activation Key field. \r\n If you access Internet websites through a proxy server, click I access the internet through a proxy server, and enter its proxy address and port. (If your computer accesses the Internet through an authenticated proxy server, complete the procedure for activating without Internet access.) \r\n Click Next. \r\n Enter your email address and other registration information, and then click Next. \r\n \r\n To license the software on a computer without Internet access: \r\n \r\n \r\n On the computer you want to license, click Start > All Programs > SolarWinds > Dameware Mini Remote Control > Enter licensing information. \r\n \r\n Select This server does not have internet access, and then click Next. \r\n Click Copy Unique Machine ID. \r\n Paste the copied data into a text editor document. \r\n Transfer the document to a computer with Internet access. \r\n On the computer with Internet access, complete the following steps: Browse to https://customerportal.solarwinds.com/ , and then log into the portal with your SolarWinds customer ID and password. Locate your product, and then click Manually Register License. If the Manually Register License option is not available for your product, contact SolarWinds Customer Support . Provide the Machine ID, and then download your license key file. \r\n Transfer the license key file to the computer you want to license. \r\n Return to the Activate MRC window, browse to the license key files, and then click Next. \r\n \r\n Centralized Licensing (MRC licenses) \r\n After installing the Dameware Central Server (DamewareServer.exe), activate your license on the Central Server using the centralized licensing. After the license is activated on the Central Server, you can assign licenses to users using the Administration Console. \r\n After Central Server is running, install or upgrade Dameware Mini Remote Control applications, and choose Centralized Install in the Installers. Deactivate any pre-existing licenses on the computers you upgrade. \r\n You must request the centralized version of Dameware Mini Remote Control from your SolarWinds sales representative. \r\n To license the software on a computer with Internet access: \r\n \r\n Click Start > All Programs > SolarWinds > Dameware Server > Activate Dameware Licenses > Licensing. \r\n Click Enter Licensing information. \r\n Select I have internet access and an activation key. \r\n Access the customer portal on the SolarWinds website at: http://www.solarwinds.com/customerportal . \r\n Log in using your SolarWinds customer ID and password. \r\n Click License Management. \r\n Locate your product, choose an activation key from the Unregistered Licenses section, and then copy the activation key. \r\n If you cannot find an activation key in the Unregistered Licenses section, contact SolarWinds Customer Support . \r\n Return to the Activation window, and then enter the activation key in the Activation Key field. \r\n If you access Internet websites through a proxy server, click I access the internet through a proxy server, and enter its proxy address and port. (If your computer accesses the Internet through an authenticated proxy server, complete the procedure for activating without Internet access.) \r\n Click Next. \r\n Enter your email address and other registration information, and then click Next. \r\n \r\n To license the software on a computer without Internet access: \r\n \r\n Click Start > All Programs > SolarWinds > Dameware Server > Activate Dameware Licenses > Licensing. \r\n Click Enter Licensing information. \r\n Select This server does not have internet access, and then click Next. \r\n Click Copy Unique Machine ID. \r\n Paste the copied data into a text editor document. \r\n Transfer the document to a computer with Internet access. \r\n On the computer with Internet access, complete the following steps: Browse to http://www.solarwinds.com/customerportal , and then log into the portal with your SolarWinds customer ID and password. Locate your product, and then click Manually Register License. If the Manually Register License option is not available for your product, contact SolarWinds Customer Support . \r\n Transfer the license key file to the Central Server. \r\n Return to the Activation window, browse to the license key file, and then click Next. \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n End of life \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n Version \r\n EoL announcement \r\n EoE effective date \r\n EoL effective date \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n 12.3.2 \r\n March 31, 2026 : End-of-Life (EoL) announcement &ndash; Customers on Dameware version 12.3.2 or earlier should begin transitioning to the latest version of Dameware. \r\n June 30, 2026 : End-of-Engineering (EoE) &ndash; Service releases, bug fixes, workarounds, and service packs for Dameware version 12.3.2 or earlier will no longer actively be supported by SolarWinds. \r\n June 30, 2027 : End-of-Life (EoL) &ndash; SolarWinds will no longer provide technical support for Dameware version 12.3.2. \r\n \r\n 12.3.1 \r\n March 31, 2026 : End-of-Life (EoL) announcement &ndash; Customers on Dameware version 12.3.1 or earlier should begin transitioning to the latest version of Dameware. \r\n June 30, 2026 : End-of-Engineering (EoE) &ndash; Service releases, bug fixes, workarounds, and service packs for Dameware version 12.3.1 or earlier will no longer actively be supported by SolarWinds. \r\n June 30, 2027 : End-of-Life (EoL) &ndash; SolarWinds will no longer provide technical support for Dameware version 12.3.1. \r\n \r\n 12.3 \r\n March 31, 2026 : End-of-Life (EoL) announcement &ndash; Customers on Dameware version 12.3 or earlier should begin transitioning to the latest version of Dameware. \r\n June 30, 2026 : End-of-Engineering (EoE) &ndash; Service releases, bug fixes, workarounds, and service packs for Dameware version 12.3 or earlier will no longer actively be supported by SolarWinds. \r\n June 30, 2027 : End-of-Life (EoL) &ndash; SolarWinds will no longer provide technical support for Dameware version 12.3. \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n See the End of Life Policy for information about SolarWinds product life cycle phases. To see EoL dates for earlier Dameware versions, see\r\n Dameware release history . \r\n \r\n \r\n Legal notices \r\n &copy; 2026 SolarWinds Worldwide, LLC. All rights reserved. \r\n This document may not be reproduced by any means nor modified, decompiled, disassembled, published or distributed, in whole or in part, or translated to any electronic medium or other means without the prior written consent of SolarWinds. All right, title, and interest in and to the software, services, and documentation are and shall remain the exclusive property of SolarWinds, its affiliates, and/or its respective licensors. \r\n SOLARWINDS DISCLAIMS ALL WARRANTIES, CONDITIONS, OR OTHER TERMS, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, STATUTORY OR OTHERWISE, ON THE DOCUMENTATION, INCLUDING WITHOUT LIMITATION NONINFRINGEMENT, ACCURACY, COMPLETENESS, OR USEFULNESS OF ANY INFORMATION CONTAINED HEREIN. IN NO EVENT SHALL SOLARWINDS, ITS SUPPLIERS, NOR ITS LICENSORS BE LIABLE FOR ANY DAMAGES, WHETHER ARISING IN TORT, CONTRACT OR ANY OTHER LEGAL THEORY, EVEN IF SOLARWINDS HAS BEEN ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES. \r\n The SolarWinds, SolarWinds & Design, Orion, and THWACK trademarks are the exclusive property of SolarWinds Worldwide, LLC or its affiliates, are registered with the U.S. Patent and Trademark Office, and may be registered or pending registration in other countries. All other SolarWinds trademarks, service marks, and logos may be common law marks or are registered or pending registration. All other trademarks mentioned herein are used for identification purposes only and are trademarks of (and may be registered trademarks) of their respective companies. \r\n \r\n \n \r\n \r\n \r\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n \n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n SolarWinds was founded by IT professionals solving complex problems in the simplest way, and we have carried that spirit forward since 1999. We take pride in relentlessly listening to our customers to develop a deeper understanding of the challenges they face. Our digital agility solutions are built to help companies of any size accelerate business transformation today and into the future. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n COMPANY \n INVESTORS \n CAREER CENTER \n RESOURCE CENTER \n EMAIL PREFERENCE CENTER \n \n \n FOR CUSTOMERS \n FOR GOVERNMENT \n GDPR RESOURCE CENTER \n SOLARWINDS TRUST CENTER \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Legal Documents \n Privacy \n California Privacy Rights \n Security Information \n Documentation & Uninstall Information \n Sitemap \n \n \n © 2026 SolarWinds Worldwide, LLC. All rights reserved. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \r\n \r\n\r\n"
