ker/desktop-vpnkit-controller:v5.0 docker/desktop-containerd-registry-mirror:v0.0.5 docker/desktop-cloud-provider-kind:v0.8.0 Bug fixes and enhancements For all platforms Fixed Docker Hub model pulls failing on proxy-only networks where local DNS could not resolve the authentication endpoint. Fixed Docker Desktop staying on the Starting page after Docker Engine had started. Fixes docker/desktop-feedback#685 Fixed diagnose gather on slow or stopped VMs by capping the VM start wait to 120 seconds. Improved responsiveness of error dialogs. Fixed moving the disk image to another volume failing when the copy took more than 5 minutes. Fixed uncaught Request aborted errors each time the engine stopped. For Mac Removed the com.docker.vmnetd privileged helper. A helper installed by a previous version is uninstalled automatically, and the install vmnetd option of the command line installer is gone. For Windows Added Docker VMM to the Clean up data dialog. Fixed WSL error code parsing so that users running newer WSL versions (3.0.x) receive accurate, actionable recovery instructions instead of a generic error message. Fixed the Docker VMM backend option on Windows ARM64 to appear correctly disabled with an explanation in settings, and automatically fall back to WSL 2 during install or upgrade. Fixed an intermittent Being used by another process error on the desktop-linux Docker context file when the engine started. Fixed file sharing treating a directory as shared, or as allowed by Settings Management, when its name only started with that of a shared or allowed directory (e.g. C:\\foobar for C:\\foo ). Allowed file share entries now match whole directory names only. Fixed an issue where processes started in the Docker Desktop terminal could be left running after closing the terminal. Added support for running docker and docker compose from WSL 2 distros when Docker VMM is the engine, including bind mounts of files on Windows drives such as /mnt/c . Fixed Docker VMM re-enabling the WSL feature on update and showing a Press any key to install WSL prompt when WSL is uninstalled. Fixes docker/desktop-feedback#775 . Security Fixed CVE-2026-98432 , a use-after-free in the Linux kernel's IPv4 TCP handling. Fixed CVE-2026-112917 where a container on the WSL 2 backend could bypass the AF_VSOCK restriction. Requires WSL 3.0.3 or later. 4.97.0 2026-10-26 Download Docker Desktop Windows \n( checksum ) Windows ARM Early Access \n( checksum ) Mac with Apple chip \n( checksum ) Mac with Intel chip \n( checksum ) Debian \n-\n RPM \n-\n Arch \n( checksum ) Bug fixes and enhancements For all platforms Fixed a spurious Resource Saver error when signing out while sign-in enforcement is enabled. Fixed diagnostics collection being slow when the backend is unresponsive, reducing worst-case wait time from several minutes to approximately 3 seconds. Fixed reliability issues with the container exec terminal: closing a container no longer triggers spurious error reports, and terminal resize now works correctly on startup. Fixed an issue where the Date header in Docker API responses was incorrect after Docker Desktop entered Resource Saver mode. Added the -e / --env flag to docker pass run for setting environment variables, including se:// secret references. Fixed docker pass set printing \"context canceled\" on Ctrl-C at the value prompt. Improved responsiveness when searching the Images , Containers and Volumes lists. Fixed an unhandled error when viewing the files of a Compose project whose config file no longer exists. For Mac Fixed adding Docker Desktop commands to the PATH failing for fish users without a ~/.config/fish directory. Added a setting to allow privileged ports (1-1024) to be exposed to other machines on the LAN. For Windows Added a Docker VMM (Beta) backend option to the Windows installer. Fixed an issue on Windows where a slow WSL version check asked to update WSL. Fixed Docker VMM requiring a Docker Desktop restart to share a new bind-mount directory from the host. Fixed WSL installer errors (e.g. Wsl/CallMsi/ ) being misidentified as disk-related failures, preventing misleading 'disk file has been deleted' recovery messages. Fixed Docker Desktop becoming unresponsive, with docker commands hanging and Quit not working, after the disk filled up or, on Windows, after the backend's console host process exited. Fixes docker/desktop-feedback#429 and docker/desktop-feedback#699 . Fixed an issue where the installer rejected --backend=docker-vmm when combined with --user flag or Microsoft Store installs. Fixed factory reset to stop Docker engines before deleting data, surface cleanup failures as an error dialog, and clean up custom data-root directories. Fixed Windows containers failing to start with a \"Path contains symlink\" error on callback.sock . Fixed a bug where the installer could leave a file under C:\\ProgramData\\DockerDesktop with no permissions at all, making it unreadable to diagnostics and to later installs. Fixed a bug where the disk image location could not be moved back to a folder it had previously been moved out of. Fixes docker/desktop-feedback#565 . Fixed a bug where a failed update could put back Start Menu and desktop shortcuts that had been deleted on purpose. --user mode is now the default for new Docker Desktop .EXE installations. Security Addressed CVE-2026-114409 , where Docker Desktop could write third-party API keys and OAuth access tokens in cleartext to local application logs and diagnostics bundles. This release also cleans up existing host logs and crash dumps. These OAuth tokens are not Docker account tokens. If you've generated or shared diagnostics bundles with Docker Desktop 4.96.x or earlier, or kept copies of Docker Desktop logs elsewhere, delete or sanitize them. Addressed CVE-2026-99999 , a kernel vulnerability where a container could exploit bad IPv4 checksum metadata via TUN or AF_PACKET to corrupt the VM's network stack. 4.96.3 2026-10-22 Download Docker Desktop Windo