 whatsoever, there's unchecked_add to explicitly opt-in to a C-like \"just do whatever the machine feels like\". You can still do everything you can with C. It it just an explicit choice, rather than an implicit platform-dependent mechanism you might forget about. reply MFHava 52 minutes ago | root | parent | prev | next [–] \n > Profiles Contrary to Contracts, which at least managed to get consensus in WG21, I very much doubt that Profiles will get consensus. reply ho_schi 1 hour ago | root | parent | prev | next [–] \n Yep. Safety and simplicity need to be the priority. reply Maxatar 8 hours ago | parent | prev | next [–] \n Yes that's right, and from following some threads on reddit about this, he used some really dirty tactics to get it to fail, like scheduling certain snap elections to happen with very short notice at times of the day when people who would oppose his point of view would likely be asleep. reply raegis 6 hours ago | root | parent | next [–] \n > ...at times of the day when people who would oppose his point of view would likely be asleep. Stroustrup is 75 years old. This is not only hard to believe because of his age, but also because it requires that people who oppose his views somehow have distinct sleeping patterns from ones who agree with his views. Weird, man. reply hdjrudni 6 hours ago | root | parent | next [–] \n > that people who oppose his views somehow have distinct sleeping patterns from ones who agree with his views. Not weird if they're mostly from different continents. When I saw him a year or so ago he said he wasn't happy with how things were going, but never alluded to a coup. But it's his language, so good for him. reply MFHava 50 minutes ago | root | parent | next [–] \n > it's his language It most definitely is not and hasn't been in decades. A major problem is that some people still put his views on a pedestal, acting like he has a clean track record with his ideas, which he definitely has not - no language designer has ... r