  "text": " \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n Tencent releases Hy4, a powerful frontier AI model introducing visual understanding and computer use - SiliconANGLE \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n Skip to content \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n [the voice of enterprise and emerging tech] \n\n \n OUR NETWORK \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n search \n \n \n \n Search SiliconANGLE \n \n \n search \n Submit search \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n THE SILICONANGLE 120 \n \n Market Data Provided by \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Search SiliconANGLE \n \n \n search \n Submit search \n \n \n \n \n\n Home \n TechForward \n Cloud \n \n Cloud Native \n \n \n AI \n Security \n Infra \n Blockchain \n Big Data \n Emerging Tech \n AWS Marketplace Newsroom \n Policy \n Apps \n Iot \n Women In Tech \n theCUBE Research \n Special Reports \n Video Exclusives \n CUBE SPECIAL FEATURES \n RECENT CUBE EVENTS \n AWARDS \n More AWS Marketplace Newsroom Policy Apps Iot Women In Tech theCUBE Research Special Reports Video Exclusives CUBE SPECIAL FEATURES RECENT CUBE EVENTS AWARDS Sign In \n \n \n THE SILICONANGLE 120 \n \n Market Data Provided by \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n\t\n \n\n \n SHARE \n\n \n\t\n \n \n \n \n \n UPDATED 11:05 EST / NOVEMBER 04 2026 \n \n \n\n \n \n AI \n \n \n\n \n Tencent releases Hy4, a powerful frontier AI model introducing visual understanding and computer use \n \n \n \n \n \n by Kyt Dotson \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n Tencent Holdings Ltd.  today  introduced Hy4 , a new large language model that adds computer-use capabilities for the first time, using advanced visual understanding, reasoning and tool-calling to deliver long-horizon agentic performance. \n The company said the model marks a significant leap in performance over its Hy4 Preview, which  arrived Aug. 28 , weighing in at 770 billion parameters with 49 billion active parameters. Both provide a 1 million-token context window, putting it in the same range as current open-weights frontier models from European and Chinese developers, including Mistral AI SAS, Beijing Moonshot Technology Co. Ltd. and Z.AI Co. Ltd. \n The company said it substantially scaled up both pre-training and post-training, reporting gains over the preview version in instruction following, long-context understanding, agentic long-horizon tasks and deep research. Tencent also identified excessive reasoning and over-verification during the previous version’s “thinking” processes. \n The new model focuses heavily on real-world productivity for workplace collaboration, human experience and professional work. The company said it optimized long-context learning capabilities to understand complex information, including web development, document summarization, visual creative tasks, document presentation, and more. \n The company added that it also enhanced its capability for front-end and game development, high-complexity tasks that include intricate business logic, state management and orchestration. Some models struggle with producing stateful, elegant and beautiful user interfaces that are visually polished and also fully functional. \n It is not uncommon for professional game developers, industry engineers and amateur vibe coders to use AI models as part of their work. However, a recent spate has had coders begin to reproduce, reverse-engineer and clone older and semi-recent video games. That prompted Anthropic PBC to block Claude Code and its underlying Opus 5.5 model from assisting in these tasks. \n The company said it integrated deeply with major engines such as Unreal Engine, Unity and Godot, giving it the capability to support complex game logic and multiplayer implementations. Compared wit the preview, Tencent said, Hy4 improved by 19.1 percent in the GameDev bench and 9.8 percent in GameLogic benchmarks, although the actual baseline numbers remain internal and weren’t released. \n To advance scientific reasoning, Tencent advanced the next stage of Recursive Self-Improvement to enhance research and development capabilities. Using the Hyra 2.0 harness, an autonomous AI research agent system, the model optimized the pre-training infrastructure for smaller models sharing the same architecture. \n The model is currently available on Tencent Cloud TokenHub, WorkBuddy, CodeBuddy, Yuanbao, WeCom’s AI Assistant, Ima and more. It can also be accessed via third-party sources such as OpenRouter, Hermes and OpenCode. The company added that, despite its significant enhancements over Hy4 Preview, it kept costs low, maintaining the same pricing at around 90 cents per million input tokens, $2.70 per million output tokens and 4.5 cents per million cached input tokens. \n The Flash version of the model is scheduled for release soon to deliver greater cost efficiency for users. The company also said it intends to release the model weights and system cards in coming days. \n Image: Tencent \n \n A message from John Furrier, co-founder of SiliconANGLE: \n Support our mission to keep content open and free by engaging with theCUBE community. Join theCUBE’s Alumni Trust Network , where technology leaders connect, share intelligence and create opportunities. \n \n 15M+ viewers of theCUBE videos , powering conversations across AI, cloud, cybersecurity and more \n 11.4k+ theCUBE alumni — Connect with more than 11,400 tech and business leaders shaping the future through a unique trusted-based network \n \n \n \n \n Are you an AWS customer?  Support SiliconANGLE financially by buying your AWS services from our Marketplace portal page and links: https://siliconangle.com/aws-marketplace/ \n \n About SiliconANGLE Media \n \n SiliconANGLE Media is a recognized leader in digital media innovation, uniting breakthrough technology, strategic insights and real-time audience engagement. As the parent company of SiliconANGLE , theCUBE Network , theCUBE Research , CUBE365 , theCUBE AI and theCUBE SuperStudios — with flagship locations in Silicon Valley and the New York Stock Exchange — SiliconANGLE Media operates at the intersection of media, technology and AI. \n \n \n Founded by tech visionaries John Furrier and Dave Vellante, SiliconANGLE Media has built a dynamic ecosystem of industry-leading digital media brands that reach 15+ million elite tech professionals. Our new proprietary theCUBE AI Video Cloud is breaking ground in audience interaction, leveraging theCUBEai.com neural network to help technology companies make data-driven decisions and stay at the forefront of industry conversations. \n \n \n\n LATEST STORIES Customers are pulling data back into the Oracle database as agents demand real-time access Oracle urges database customers to prepare for quantum security risks University AI’s biggest challenge? Scaling research without losing control Smartsheet AI-powered platform bridges gap between planning and results VMware gets simpler AI deployment and low-cost version for basic private clouds Descope launches Envoy to let consumer apps accept personal AI agents as users LATEST STORIES Customers are pulling data back into the Oracle database as agents demand real-time access AI - BY RYAN STEVENS . 18 MINUTES AGO Oracle urges database customers to prepare for quantum security risks SECURITY - BY JONATHAN ANTHONY . 21 MINUTES AGO University AI’s biggest challenge? Scaling research without losing control SECURITY - BY RYAN STEVENS . 2 HOURS AGO Smartsheet AI-powered platform bridges gap between planning and results APPS - BY PAUL GILLIN . 3 HOURS AGO VMware gets simpler AI deployment and low-cost version for basic private clouds CLOUD - BY PAUL GILLIN . 3 HOURS AGO Descope launches Envoy to let consumer apps accept personal AI agents as users SECURITY - BY DUNCAN RILEY . 6 HOURS AGO \n\n \n \n \n CUBE EVENT COVERAGE help_outline \n LATEST FROM THECUBE Customers are pulling data back into the Oracle database as agents demand real-time access Oracle urges database customers to prepare for quantum security risks University AI’s biggest challenge? Scaling research without losing control IBM puts agentic workloads at the heart of its AI operating model Enterprise architecture: Dell and Microsoft integrate hybrid AI \n DIVE INTO DAVE VELLANTE’S BREAKING ANALYSIS SERIES help_outline Can enterprise AI pay for the boom? Micron’s memory boom: Is the industry's cyclicality really ending? ServiceNow AI Control Tower: Selling a penthouse while building the frame The AI control gap: Who gets to say ‘It’s safe'? Nvidia’s scale-in play: Controlling agents is the next infrastructure priority \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Sign Up for Our Weekly Newsletter SUBSCRIBE \n \n UPCOMING CUBE EVENTS SEE MORE \n RECENT CUBE EVENTS monday.com Elevate 2026 Intuit Connect 2026 EVOLVE26 AI Cybersecurity & Resilience Summit 2026 IBM's AI Operating Model 2026 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n PRIVACY POLICY \n TERMS \n ABOUT US \n CONTACT US \n BRAND GUIDELINES \n Send us a News tip \n \n\n \n Join our community \n \n \n \n \n theCUBE\n \n \n \n \n \n theCUBE Research\n \n \n \n \n\n \n &copy; 2026 SiliconANGLE Media Inc. All rights reserved. \n\n \n \n\n \n × \n Send us a news tip \n \n \n \n Send us a News Tip \n \n Comments This field is for validation purposes and should be left unchanged. Name * \n \n \n \n First \n \n \n \n \n Last \n \n \n Type of Pitch * Consumer or Enterprise? Enterprise Startup News Emerging Technology Email * \n \n What's your story? * File Max. file size: 244 MB. CAPTCHA \n \n 