 XMX matrix-engine kernels on SYCL, cooperative GEMMs, Q2_K/Q3_K weights and a lightning indexer on OpenCL, subgroup reductions and src1 precision control on Vulkan, and a restructured HTP backend with new repacking and fusion machinery on Hexagon. ZDNN gained flash attention and WebGPU gained Q2_0. \n API changes \n \n New GGML_OP_TOP_K_MASK op and ggml_top_k_mask() - fused top-k sparse attention mask over picks, blocks and extra cells llama/30640 \n New ggml_prec_get_acc() / ggml_prec_get_src() to query the accumulator and per-source precision of a compute node llama/30656 \n ggml_mul_mat_id and ggml_add_id accept -1 as an index: the slot is skipped and the output row is zeroed llama/26631 \n RPC protocol patch version bumped to 8.0.1 for the new op ( GGML_OP_COUNT is now 102) \n \n Core changes \n \n ggml_scale now accepts non-contiguous row views instead of requiring contiguous input llama/31146 \n SUM supports non-contiguous inputs on CPU, CUDA, Vulkan and WebGPU llama/28851 \n MUL_MAT_ID / ADD_ID skip the work for -1 indices in all major backends llama/26631 \n Meta backend: per-expert token scaling for MoE down projections, plus split-state support for the new masking op llama/30861 llama/31081 \n Fix potential counter overflow in ggml_time_ms / ggml_time_us on Windows llama/30969 \n ARGMAX added to the ops that may expand during allocation, avoiding undersized buffers llama/30862 \n RPC: handle oversized RDMA transfers and std::length_error on message receive instead of aborting llama/30399 llama/31204 \n \n Backend changes \n CPU \n \n New CONCAT implementation as a single row kernel covering all types llama/31179 \n KleidiAI: Q8_0 SVE dotprod GEMV and SVE i8mm GEMM kernels, with runtime SVE-i8MM feature detection llama/30808 \n Vectorized v_silu and v_expf , NEON fp32->fp16 conversion, fp32 gelu_quick / geglu_quick without the fp16 table llama/30791 llama/30505 llama/30737 \n Reduce AVX2 tiled accumulators together to cut register pressure in the tiled matmul path llama/30296 \n \n CUDA / HIP \n \n MoE: fused grouped-experts top-k, plus a dedicated fusion path for large expert counts (up to 384) llama/29181 llama/31288 \n Fuse the FFN gate/up matmuls with GLU in MMQ using interleaved gate/up rows; fuse MRoPE with SET_ROWS llama/29948 llama/31025 \n Chunk CUDA graph launches to amortize the launch overhead; clear graphs after a legacy memory pool flush llama/30804 llama/26771 \n Faster MMVQ for low-bit types; MMQ Stream-K capped at available work; DP4A MMQ tile height aligned to the warp size llama/30517 llama/30553 llama/30837 \n SSM_CONV supports kernel size 7; RMS_NORM variants loading float4 and keeping x in registers llama/30873 llama/29720 \n HIP: byte-permute Q1_0 unpacking with a portable fallback; fix bf16 WMMA operand type for gfx11/gfx12 llama/29927 llama/30915 llama/30885 \n Fix shared-memory WAR hazard in vectorized flash attention and a tile-width selection bug in the matmul reduction llama/30573 llama/30836 \n Limit the maximum pinned host buffer size to 4 GB llama/30449 \n \n Metal \n \n Implement TOP_K_MASK llama/31230 \n Optimized ARGMAX and POOL_1D kernels; removed the amax rescaling from the MoE matmul llama/30862 llama/30924 \n Fix 32-bit overflow in large matrix output offsets llama/30072 \n Fix missing MoE kernel variant for 9 experts per token, and a moe_reduce fusion race when dst aliases its inputs llama/30699 llama/30795 \n Fix memory leaks and cleanup logic in the GPU capture path llama/30890 \n \n Vulkan \n \n Support the src1 precision attribute on matmul ops, configurable through the standard precision setters llama/30656 \n RMS_NORM rewritten with subgroup reductions llama/29882 \n Small matmul tiles now use one warp tile per subgroup; larger conv3d tile for coopmat2; clamp coopmat1 int8 prefetch llama/30106 llama/29920 llama/30283 \n Allow dim-3 broadcast in MUL_MAT and fix gpu-visible host memory handling llama/31239 llama/30468 \n \n SYCL \n \n Add graph record and replay to reduce per-op launch overhead llama/28725 \n Restore ESIMD kernels on the FFN path and rework multi-column matmul on Intel XMX matrix engines llama/30239 llama/29864 \n Faster dequantization: fast Q8 path, wide stores for Q4_K/Q5_K, merged fp16/fp32 dequant switches, templated MMVQ/concat launches llama/30775 llama/29696 llama/30740 llama/31013 llama/31008 \n set_tensor_2d for faster tensor-split (KV-cache) loading; bound weight-reorder scratch memory to 32 MiB llama/30358 llama/31062 \n Reordered-quantized weights: fix GET_ROWS , fix prompt-processing regression, support reordered Q8_0 MoE weights llama/30430 llama/30374 llama/29337 \n Flash attention: explicit dependencies instead of host waits in the MKL path, fix crash on mismatched head dimensions llama/30684 llama/30286 llama/30812 \n Fix CONV_2D results for non-contiguous input and an IQ3 crash llama/30363 llama/30604 \n \n OpenCL \n \n Initial Q2_K and Q3_K support across gemv/gemm/mul-mat/mul-id kernels, including MoE variants llama/30999 llama/31172 \n New TOP_K and lightning indexer kernels for sparse attention llama/31026 \n New ops: depthwise CONV_2D , IM2COL_3D , ARGMAX , i32 GET_ROWS and i32/f32 CPY llama/30900 llama/30895 llama/30897 llama/30756 \n More DP4A GEMM coverage: cooperative kernels for Q4_0/Q4_K/Q6_K, vectorized activation loads, extra small-batch variants [llama/30741]( https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull ... \n \n Read more \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Assets \n 2 \n \n \n \n \n \n Loading \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n Uh oh!\n \n There was an error while loading. Please reload this page . \n \n\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n \n \n --> \n \n \n \n \n \n All reactions \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n v0.27.0 \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n v0.27.0 \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n Compare \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n Choose a tag to compare\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Sorry, something went wrong. \n \n \n \n \n \n Filter\n \n \n \n \n \n Loading 