  "text": " \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n Paper page - Switch-SWE: Do Coding Agents Hold Focus When Switching Between Unfinished Tasks? \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n Hugging Face Models Datasets Spaces Buckets Docs Enterprise Pricing Website Tasks HuggingChat Collections Languages Organizations Community Blog Posts Daily Papers Hardware Learn Discord Forum GitHub Solutions Team & Enterprise Hugging Face PRO Enterprise Support Inference Providers Inference Endpoints Storage Buckets Log In Sign Up Switch-SWE is a repository-level benchmark for evaluating whether coding agents can resume a focus task after working on other unfinished tasks in the same repository. Each task is evaluated in matched uninterrupted and switched sessions, requiring agents to recover task-specific requirements and partial progress while avoiding cross-task confusion.</p>\\n<p>The benchmark provides 200 focus tasks from 19 Python repositories, 400 matched session specifications, and executable verifiers. Across seven coding agents, task switching reduces focus-task resolution by 11.5 percentage points on average. A plug-in context-management module that selects relevant history and maintains task-state summaries improves completion by 5.5–15.5 percentage points on OpenCode.</p>\\n<p>🌐 Paper: <a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.02017\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.02017</a><br>🔥 Project Page: <a href=\\\"https://mqleet.github.io/Switch-Swe/\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">https://mqleet.github.io/Switch-Swe/</a><br>🕹️ Code: <a href=\\\"https://github.com/Miraclecsc/Switch-SWE\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">https://github.com/Miraclecsc/Switch-SWE</a></p>\\n\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-11-04T06:30:55.030Z\",\"author\":{\"_id\":\"6448b2f53e7b3c11be684348\",\"avatarUrl\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/6448b2f53e7b3c11be684348/QvlUQG3pWf8ZyEVBV6F7w.jpeg\",\"fullname\":\"Qianli Ma\",\"