anage vulnerabilities and keep pace with threat activity—CISA maintains the authoritative source of vulnerabilities that have been exploited in the wild. Organizations should use the KEV catalog as an input to their vulnerability management prioritization framework. Learn more about how to use the KEV catalog in your organization. Are you aware of an actively exploited vulnerability not included in the KEV Catalog? NOMINATE A NEW KEV The KEV catalog is also available in these formats: CSV JSON Print View JSON Schema (updated 09-02-2026) License \n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n Showing 1 to 20 of 1767 results \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n WordPress | WordPress Core \n \n \n \n CVE-2026-119977 \n\n \n WordPress WordPress Core Time-of-check Time-of-use (TOCTOU) Race Condition Vulnerability: WordPress WordPress Core contains a time-of-check time-of-use (TOCTOU) race condition vulnerability that could allow unauthenticated attackers to execute code on the server during the upgrade window. This is due to predictable, web-accessible staging paths used during full-package core upgrades.\n \n \n \n \n Related CWE: \n CWE-367 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Known To Be Used in Ransomware Campaigns?\n \n Unknown\n \n \n \n Forensic triage required per BOD 26-04: \n \n Yes \n \n \n \n \n Date Added: \n 2026-11-03 \n Due Date: \n 2026-11-06 \n \n \n \n \n \n Action: Apply mitigations in accordance with vendor instructions, ensuring compliance with CISA’s BOD 26-04 Prioritizing Security Updates Based on Risk (see URL in Notes) guidance and CISA’s “Forensics Triage Requirements” (see URL in Notes). Follow applicable BOD 26-04 guidance for cloud services or discontinue use of the product if mitigations are unavailable. Stakeholders are responsible for evaluating each asset's internet exposure and ensuring adherence to BOD 26-04 patching guidelines.\n \n \n Additional Notes \n \n https://wordpress.org/news/2026/10/wordpress-7-1-4 ; https://www.wordfence.com/threat-intel/vulnerabilities/wordpress-core/wordpress-core-470-713-unauthenticated-upgrade-window-staged-installer-remote-code-execution ; BOD 26-04: https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk ; Forensics Triage Requirements: https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-implementation-guidance-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk ; https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-119977 \n \n \n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n Ivanti | Connect Secure \n \n \n \n CVE-2026-111357 \n\n \n Ivanti Connect Secure Missing Authentication for Critical Function Vulnerability: Ivanti Connect Secure contains a missing authentication for critical function vulnerability that could allow a local authenticated attacker to escalate their privileges. This vulnerability can be chained with CVE-2026-104935 and CVE-2026-118527.\n \n \n \n \n Related CWEs: \n CWE-306 | \n CWE-862 | \n CWE-345 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Known To Be Used in Ransomware Campaigns?\n \n Unknown\n \n \n \n Forensic triage required per BOD 26-04: \n \n Yes \n \n \n \n \n Date Added: \n 2026-10-30 \n Due Date: \n 2026-11-02 \n \n \n \n \n \n Action: Apply mitigations in accordance with vendor instructions, ensuring compliance with CISA’s BOD 26-04 Prioritizing Security Updates Based on Risk (see URL in Notes) guidance and CISA’s “Forensics Triage Requirements” (see URL in Notes). Follow applicable BOD 26-04 guidance for cloud services or discontinue use of the product if mitigations are unavailable. Stakeholders are responsible for evaluating each asset's internet exposure and ensuring adherence to BOD 26-04 patching guidelines.\n \n \n Additional Notes \n \n https://hub.ivanti.com/s/article/Security-Advisory-Ivanti-Connect-Secure-CVE-2026-104935?language=en_US ; https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/alerts/2026/10/13/cisa-urges-patching-newly-exploited-vulnerability-ivanti-connect-secure ; BOD 26-04: https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk ; Forensics Triage Requirements: https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-implementation-guidance-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk ; https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-111357 \n \n \n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n Ivanti | Connect Secure \n \n \n \n CVE-2026-118527 \n\n \n Ivanti Connect Secure Generation of Predictable Numbers or Identifiers Vulnerability: Ivanti Connect Secure contains a generation of predictable numbers or identifiers vulnerability that allows a remote authenticated attacker to upload files with attacker-controlled content to a known location on disk. This vulnerability can be chained with CVE-2026-104935 and CVE-2026-111357.\n \n \n \n \n Related CWE: \n CWE-340 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Known To Be Used in Ransomware Campaigns?\n \n Unknown\n \n \n \n Forensic triage required per BOD 26-04: \n \n No \n \n \n \n \n Date Added: \n 2026-10-30 \n Due Date: \n 2026-11-13 \n \n \n \n \n \n Action: Apply mitigations in accordance with vendor instructions, ensuring compliance with CISA’s BOD 26-04 Prioritizing Security Updates Based on Risk (see URL in Notes) guidance and CISA’s “Forensics Triage Requirements” (see URL in Notes). Follow applicable BOD 26-04 guidance for cloud services or discontinue use of the product if mitigations are unavailable. Stakeholders are responsible for evaluating each asset's internet exposure and ensuring adherence to BOD 26-04 patching guidelines.\n \n \n Additional Notes \n \n https://hub.ivanti.com/s/article/Security-Advisory-Ivanti-Connect-Secure-CVE-2026-104935?language=en_US ; ; BOD 26-04: https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk ; Forensics Triage Requirements: https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-implementation-guidance-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk ; https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-118527 \n \n \n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n Cisco | Secure Firewall ASA Software and Cisco Secure FTD Software \n \n \n \n CVE-2026-76418 \n\n \n Cisco Secure Firewall ASA Software and Cisco Secure FTD Software Unchecked Return Value to NULL Pointer Dereference Vulnerability: Cisco Secure Firewall ASA Software and Cisco Secure FTD Software contains an unchecked return value to NULL pointer dereference vulnerability that could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to cause the device to reload unexpectedly, resulting in a denial of service (DoS) condition.\n \n \n \n \n Related CWE: \n CWE-690 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Known To Be Used in Ransomware Campaigns?\n \n Unknown\n \n \n \n Forensic triage required per BOD 26-04: \n \n No \n \n \n \n \n Date Added: \n 2026-10-29 \n Due Date: \n 2026-11-01 \n \n \n \n \n \n Action: Apply mitigations in accordance with vendor instructions, ensuring compliance with CISA’s BOD 26-04 Prioritizing Security Updates Based on Risk (see URL in Notes) guidance and CISA’s “Forensics Triage Requirements” (see URL in Notes). Follow applicable BOD 26-04 guidance for cloud services or discontinue use of the product if mitigations are unavailable. Stakeholders are responsible for evaluating each asset's internet exposure and ensuring adherence to BOD 26-04 patching guidelines.\n \n \n Additional Notes \n \n https://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/content/CiscoSecurityAdvisory/cisco-sa-asaftd-tunnel-dos-s6mgkb75 ; ; BOD 26-04: https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk ; Forensics Triage Requirements: https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-implementation-guidance-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk ; https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-76418 \n \n \n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n GitLab | Community Edition and Enterprise Edition \n \n \n \n CVE-2026-97229 \n\n \n GitLab Community Edition and Enterprise Edition Integer Overflow or Wraparound Vulnerability: GitLab Community Edition and Enterprise Edition contain a integer overflow or wraparound vulnerability that could allow an unauthenticated user to execute arbitrary code on the GitLab server via a specially crafted regular expression in a CI/CD configuration, due to insufficient regular expression validation.\n \n \n \n \n Related CWE: \n CWE-190 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Known To Be Used in Ransomware Campaigns?\n \n Unknown\n \n \n \n Forensic triage required per BOD 26-04: \n \n Yes \n \n \n \n \n Date Added: \n 2026-10-29 \n Due Date: \n 2026-11-01 \n \n \n \n \n \n Action: Apply mitigations in accordance with vendor instructions, ensuring compliance with CISA’s BOD 26-04 Prioritizing Security Updates Based on Risk (see URL in Notes) guidance and CISA’s “Forensics Triage Requirements” (see URL in Notes). Follow applicable BOD 26-04 guidance for cloud services or discontinue use of the product if mitigations are unavailable. Stakeholders are responsible for evaluating each asset's internet exposure and ensuring adherence to BOD 26-04 patching guidelines.\n \n \n Additional Notes \n \n Other products can potentially be affected by the same underlying Ruby/Onigmo Integer Overflow issue in CI/CD Regular Expression Compiler. For more information please see: https://www.ruby-lang.org/en/news/2026/10/23/regexp-fixes-for-gitlab-cves ; https://docs.gitlab.com/releases/patches/patch-release-gitlab-19-4-2-released/ ; BOD 26-04: https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk ; Forensics Triage Requirements: https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/directives/bod-26-04-implementation-guidance-prioritizing-security-updates-based-risk ; https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-97229 \n \n \n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n \n \n \n Linux | Kernel \n \n \n \n CVE-2026-46300 \n\n \n Linux Kernel Missing Initialization of a Variable Vulnerability: Linux Kernel contains a missing initialization of a variable vulnerability that could allow for unintended modificatio