  "text": " \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n Paper page - ToolSpace: Scaling Tool-Centric Environment Synthesis for Long-Horizon Agents \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n \n \n \n Hugging Face Models Datasets Spaces Buckets Docs Enterprise Pricing Website Tasks HuggingChat Collections Languages Organizations Community Blog Posts Daily Papers Hardware Learn Discord Forum GitHub Solutions Team & Enterprise Hugging Face PRO Enterprise Support Inference Providers Inference Endpoints Storage Buckets Log In Sign Up Happy to share our latest work on agent environment synthesis:</p>\\n<p>🌟 ToolSpace: Scaling Tool-Centric Environment Synthesis for Long-Horizon Agents</p>\\n<p>Most existing environment synthesis methods are data-centric: they first build the underlying database, then synthesize tools and tasks. Tool interfaces easily drift from reality, and it is hard to form tasks that span environments.</p>\\n<p>ToolSpace takes the opposite approach. It first collects tools from real call traces, then chains real tool sets into a tool universe, and finally synthesizes the underlying database on demand. This preserves authenticity while flexibly generating verifiable tasks across any environment × any tool.</p>\\n<p>💡 Key methods<br>1️⃣ Tool universe exploration: mine tool dependencies from real traces and link them into a tool-world graph; synthesize databases only for environments that change state.<br>2️⃣ Verifiable task synthesis: walk the graph with state-aware traversal and backtracking, decompile executable tool chains into tasks and verification scripts, and keep environment state continuous. The same chain can yield high-quality SFT data and mixed-environment RL data.<br>3️⃣ Harder evaluation benchmarks: ToolSpace seamlessly upgrades two frontier benchmarks into AutomationBench Pro and τ³-Bench Banking Pro. Strong existing models all score below 40, setting a harder bar for the field.</p>\\n<p>📊 Experiments<br>✅ We evaluate ToolSpace-8B, 35B, and 744B on 7 long-horizon tool benchmarks. ToolSpace-744B averages 56.6, on par with Claude Opus 5.<br>✅ ToolSpace-744B: AutomationBench 54.7, Harvey LAB 27.5, SkillsBench 67.8, OfficeQA Pro 67.1, JobBench 57.5.<br>✅ Agent performance scales as environment and data scale grow.</p>\\n<p>We welcome discussion and feedback. Code and models are open-sourced 👏👏👏</p>\\n<p>📄 Paper: <a href=\\\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2611.05036\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">https://arxiv.org/pdf/2611.05036</a><br>🌐 Project page: <a href=\\\"https://toolspace-agent.github.io/\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">https://toolspace-agent.github.io/</a><br>💻 GitHub: <a href=\\\"https://github.com/dongguanting/ToolSpace\\\" rel=\\\"nofollow\\\">https://github.com/dongguanting/ToolSpace</a><br>🤗 Hugging Face: <a href=\\\"https://huggingface.co/collections/dongguanting/toolspace\\\">https://huggingface.co/collections/dongguanting/toolspace</a></p>\\n\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-11-04T06:11:34.843Z\",\"author\":{\"_id\":\"61cd4b833dd34ba1985e0753\",\"avatarUrl\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/61cd4b833dd34ba1985e0753/BfHfrwotoMESpXZOHiIe4.png\",\"fullname\":\"KABI\",\"name\":\"dongguanting\",\"type\":\"user\",\"isPro\":false,\"isHf\":false,\"isHfAdmin\":false,\"isMod\":false,\"followerCount\":96,\"isUserFollowing\":false}},\"numEdits\":0,\"identifiedLanguage\":{\"language\":\"en\",\"probability\":0.8011598587036133},\"editors\":[\"dongguanting\"],\"editorAvatarUrls\":[\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/61cd4b833dd34ba1985e0753/BfHfrwotoMESpXZOHiIe4.png\"],\"reactions\":[],\"isReport\":false}}],\"primaryEmailConfirmed\":false,\"paper\":{\"id\":\"2611.05036\",\"authors\":[{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a67b\",\"name\":\"Guanting Dong\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a67c\",\"name\":\"Zhichao Sun\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a67d\",\"name\":\"Xinyu Yang\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a67e\",\"name\":\"Rui Wang\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a67f\",\"user\":{\"_id\":\"6aa0dbdb8efdd8def0cbd9d0\",\"avatarUrl\":\"/avatars/b823d4a97364a45c99813b28ad4c6246.svg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"Xin Deng\",\"user\":\"dxstar\",\"type\":\"user\",\"name\":\"dxstar\"},\"name\":\"Xin Deng\",\"status\":\"claimed_verified\",\"statusLastChangedAt\":\"2026-11-04T08:45:05.416Z\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a680\",\"name\":\"Jiajie Jin\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a681\",\"name\":\"Zhixiong Yang\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a682\",\"name\":\"Junhao Huang\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a683\",\"name\":\"Han Han\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a684\",\"name\":\"Mingyu Ma\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a685\",\"name\":\"Xiaotao Wang\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a686\",\"name\":\"Yuyang Hu\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a687\",\"name\":\"Xiaoshuai Song\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a688\",\"name\":\"Xiaoxi Li\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a689\",\"name\":\"Jiejun Tan\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a68a\",\"name\":\"Zhecan Wang\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a68b\",\"name\":\"Shihan Dou\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a68c\",\"name\":\"Honglin Guo\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a68d\",\"name\":\"Zhiheng Xi\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a68e\",\"name\":\"Tao Gui\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a68f\",\"name\":\"Tao Ji\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a690\",\"name\":\"Qi Zhang\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a691\",\"name\":\"Yutao Zhu\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a692\",\"name\":\"Ji-Rong Wen\",\"hidden\":false},{\"_id\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a693\",\"name\":\"Zhicheng Dou\",\"hidden\":false}],\"mediaUrls\":[\"https://cdn-uploads.huggingface.co/production/uploads/61cd4b833dd34ba1985e0753/0GFlMmuAI0fMjhCxIyrHX.mp4\"],\"publishedAt\":\"2026-11-03T00:00:00.000Z\",\"submittedOnDailyAt\":\"2026-11-04T00:00:00.000Z\",\"title\":\"ToolSpace: Scaling Tool-Centric Environment Synthesis for Long-Horizon Agents\",\"submittedOnDailyBy\":{\"_id\":\"61cd4b833dd34ba1985e0753\",\"avatarUrl\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/61cd4b833dd34ba1985e0753/BfHfrwotoMESpXZOHiIe4.png\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"KABI\",\"user\":\"dongguanting\",\"type\":\"user\",\"name\":\"dongguanting\"},\"summary\":\"Large language models are deployed as long-horizon agents that compose diverse tools across MCP services into executable workflows. Existing MCP environment-scaling methods are data-centric: they first synthesize a database and scenario, then derive tools and tasks from them. As a result, tool interfaces may not match real ones, tool compositions are not grounded in execution, and tasks rarely span more than one environment. We propose ToolSpace, a tool-centric framework that reverses this order. ToolSpace mines data, state, and retry dependencies from adjacent calls in execution traces of real MCP services and open agent corpora, using deterministic rules rather than LLM judgment, and clusters the resulting weighted tool-composition graph into environments. Databases are synthesized only for state-mutating environments, while query and stateless tools replay recorded returns. ToolSpace then performs state-aware random walks with rollback and decompiles each chain into a natural-language task with assertion-based checks, keeping only samples that replay successfully from the initial state. Applied to AutomationBench and tau3-Bench Banking, the pipeline produces harder Pro versions on which 7 frontier models drop by up to 38.2 points. Across seven long-horizon tool-use benchmarks, ToolSpace raises Qwen3.6-35B-A3B from 23.0 to 41.0 average score (43.2 with RL) and GLM-5.2 from 44.6 to 56.6, on par with Claude Opus 5. Ablations show that execution-witnessed edges clearly outperform LLM-judged ones, and performance keeps improving with data and environment scale.\",\"upvotes\":34,\"discussionId\":\"6aeacb88870269964d13a694\",\"projectPage\":\"https://toolspace-agent.github.io/\",\"githubRepo\":\"https://github.com/dongguanting/ToolSpace\",\"githubRepoAddedBy\":\"user\",\"ai_summary\":\"ToolSpace constructs realistic multi-environment tool-use benchmarks by mining execution traces, clustering tool compositions, and validating tasks through replayable state-aware random walks.\",\"ai_keywords\":[\"MCP services\",\"tool-centric framework\",\"execution traces\",\"weighted tool-composition graph\",\"state-aware random walks\",\"assertion-based checks\",\"long-horizon tool-use benchmarks\"],\"ai_summary_model\":\"thinkingmachines/Inkling-Small\",\"githubStars\":28,\"organization\":{\"_id\":\"622177ac43826d6f261f8208\",\"name\":\"RUC\",\"fullname\":\"Renmin University of China\",\"avatar\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/61ac8f8a00d01045fca0ad2f/670IAX9A2-BflqA5MiSBW.jpeg\"}},\"canReadDatabase\":false,\"canManagePapers\":false,\"canSubmit\":false,\"hasHfLevelAccess\":false,\"upvoted\":false,\"upvoters\":[{\"_id\":\"61cd4b833dd34ba1985e0753\",\"avatarUrl\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/61cd4b833dd34ba1985e0753/BfHfrwotoMESpXZOHiIe4.png\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"KABI\",\"user\":\"dongguanting\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"6812ccc194073576b7a9dbf8\",\"avatarUrl\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/6812ccc194073576b7a9dbf8/OF26xantQUz7VUZh8YgJ6.jpeg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"Pat Greener\",\"user\":\"PatDark\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"6821a2765dac8d0dbb154b50\",\"avatarUrl\":\"/avatars/a6f085922a455cb797f83f66c35bbb36.svg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"Chengjun Pan\",\"user\":\"pcj-sudo\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"6695f14df0ffd8e3a379ad61\",\"avatarUrl\":\"/avatars/cc9719e352718fc56f767d9c310cda5d.svg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"Jiajie Jin\",\"user\":\"jinjiajie\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"65b71b9e8bb894c96cc7707b\",\"avatarUrl\":\"/avatars/5e432a4efcb2932df3ed34d1c0af8567.svg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"Tao Gui (SII)\",\"user\":\"guixiaotao\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"661cf0bea4fea4a7e6e1efe6\",\"avatarUrl\":\"/avatars/dda373bd016531d3c6496adcfb8ab11d.svg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"Qiye Cai\",\"user\":\"Kle1n2\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"64760bb632369fb179586ffe\",\"avatarUrl\":\"/avatars/81bc242db1da0b63a299bc66d4d1c20c.svg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"Huijie Lv\",\"user\":\"huizhang\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"69285fd02e2c2a50642efdee\",\"avatarUrl\":\"/avatars/0f15a6ba2d21ad815c27100d6bd1243e.svg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"tttttt\",\"user\":\"13444-w\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"65082d1dffc738079cabdbae\",\"avatarUrl\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/65082d1dffc738079cabdbae/2qo2GdEGpcoGsKGMesKsb.jpeg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"XXHStudyHard\",\"user\":\"XXHStudyHard\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"669e20b7abf44e8af301e102\",\"avatarUrl\":\"/avatars/7259e6cb4d459d2be7fb53dce6482163.svg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"Dong Yichen\",\"user\":\"Dongych\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"653f1ef4aabbf15fc76a259c\",\"avatarUrl\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/653f1ef4aabbf15fc76a259c/1jJDeTOJaJIKQZ4g3i8V3.jpeg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"Hao Li\",\"user\":\"LLLeo612\",\"type\":\"user\"},{\"_id\":\"6ae9c9e39c262a300f1b8abf\",\"avatarUrl\":\"/avatars/48e5ce73da13e8092feab1d694d3c020.svg\",\"isPro\":false,\"fullname\":\"ryan\",\"user\":\"ryanxking\",\"type\":\"user\"}],\"acceptLanguages\":[\"*\"],\"dailyPaperRank\":0,\"organization\":{\"_id\":\"622177ac43826d6f261f8208\",\"name\":\"RUC\",\"fullname\":\"Renmin University of China\",\"avatar\":\"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/61ac8f8a00d01045fca0ad2f/670IAX9A2-BflqA5MiSBW.jpeg\"},\"markdownContentUrl\":\"https://huggingface.co/buckets/huggingchat/papers-content/resolve/2611/2611.05036.md\",\"query\":{}}\"> Papers arxiv:2611.05036 Copy markdown ToolSpace: Scaling Tool-Centric Environment Synthesis for Long-Horizon Agents Published on Nov 3 · Submitted by KABI on Nov 4 · Renmin University of China Upvote 34 +26 Authors: Guanting Dong , Zhichao Sun , Xinyu Yang , Rui Wang , Xin Deng , Jiajie Jin , Zhixiong Yang , Junhao Huang , Han Han , Mingyu Ma , Xiaotao Wang , Yuyang Hu , Xiaoshuai Song , Xiaoxi Li , Jiejun Tan , Zhecan Wang , Shihan Dou , Honglin Guo , Zhiheng Xi , Tao Gui , Tao Ji , Qi Zhang + 3 authors Abstract ToolSpace constructs realistic multi-environment tool-use benchmarks by mining execution traces, clustering tool compositions, and validating tasks through replayable state-aware random walks. Generated by thinkingmachines/Inkling-Small Large language models are deployed as long-horizon agents that compose diverse tools across MCP services into executable workflows. Existing MCP environment-scaling methods are data-centric: they first synthesize a database and scenario, then derive tools and tasks from them. As a result, tool interfaces may not match real ones, tool compositions are not grounded in execution, and tasks rarely span more than one environment. We propose ToolSpace, a tool-centric framework that reverses this order. ToolSpace mines data, state, and retry dependencies from adjacent calls in execution traces of real MCP services and open agent corpora, using deterministic rules rather than LLM judgment, and clusters the resulting weighted tool-composition graph into environments. Databases are synthesized only for state-mutating environments, while query and stateless tools replay recorded returns. ToolSpace then performs state-aware random walks with rollback and decompiles each chain into a natural-language task with assertion-based checks , keeping only samples that replay successfully from the initial state. Applied to AutomationBench and tau3-Bench Banking, the pipeline produces harder Pro versions on which 7 frontier models drop by up to 38.2 points. Across seven long-horizon tool-use benchmarks , ToolSpace raises Qwen3.6-35B-A3B from 23.0 to 41.0 average score (43.2 with RL) and GLM-5.2 from 44.6 to 56.6, on par with Claude Opus 5. Ablations show that execution-witnessed edges clearly outperform LLM-judged ones, and performance keeps improving with data and environment scale. View arXiv page View PDF Project page GitHub 28 Add to collection Community dongguanting Paper submitter about 14 hours ago Happy to share our latest work on agent environment synthesis: \n 🌟 ToolSpace: Scaling Tool-Centric Environment Synthesis for Long-Horizon Agents \n Most existing environment synthesis methods are data-centric: they first build the underlying database, then synthesize tools and tasks. Tool interfaces easily drift from reality, and it is hard to form tasks that span environments. \n ToolSpace takes the opposite approach. It first collects tools from real call traces, then chains real tool sets into a tool universe, and finally synthesizes the underlying database on demand. This preserves authenticity while flexibly generating verifiable tasks across any environment × any tool. \n 💡 Key methods 1️⃣ Tool universe exploration: mine tool dependencies from real traces and link them into a tool-world graph; synthesize databases only for environments that change state. 2️⃣ Verifiable task synthesis: walk the graph with state-aware traversal and backtracking, decompile executable tool chains into tasks and verification scripts, and keep environment state continuous. The same chain can yield high-quality SFT data and mixed-environment RL data. 3️⃣ Harder evaluation benchmarks: ToolSpace seamlessly upgrades two frontier benchmarks into AutomationBench Pro and τ³-Bench Banking Pro. Strong existing models all score below 40, setting a harder bar for the field. \n 📊 Experiments ✅ We evaluate ToolSpace-8B, 35B, and 744B on 7 long-horizon tool benchmarks. ToolSpace-744B averages 56.6, on par with Claude Opus 5. ✅ ToolSpace-744B: AutomationBench 54.7, Harvey LAB 27.5, SkillsBench 67.8, OfficeQA Pro 67.1, JobBench 57.5. ✅ Agent performance scales as environment and data scale grow. \n We welcome discussion and feedback. Code and models are open-sourced 👏👏👏 \n 📄 Paper: https://arxiv.org/pdf/2611.05036 🌐 Project page: https://toolspace-agent.github.io/ 💻 GitHub: https://github.com/dongguanting/ToolSpace 🤗 Hugging Face: https://huggingface.co/collections/dongguanting/toolspace \n See translation Reply Edit Preview Upload images, audio, and videos by dragging in the text input, pasting, or clicking here . Tap or paste here to upload images Comment · Sign up or log in to comment Upvote 34 +22 Get this paper in your agent: hf papers read 2611.05036 Don't have the latest CLI? curl -LsSf https://hf.co/cli/install.sh | bash Models citing this paper 3 dongguanting/ToolSpace-35B-A3B Image-Text-to-Text • 35B • Updated about 12 hours ago • 68 • 3 dongguanting/ToolSpace-8B Text Generation • 8B • Updated about 12 hours ago • 226 • 2 dongguanting/ToolSpace-744B-A40B Text Generation • 753B • Updated about 12 hours ago • 234 • 2 Datasets citing this paper 0 No dataset linking this paper Cite arxiv.org/abs/2611.05036 in a dataset README.md to link it from this page. Spaces citing this paper 0 No Space linking this paper Cite arxiv.org/abs/2611.05036 in a Space README.md to link it from this page. Collections including this paper 1 ToolSpace Collection The collection of ToolSpace • 4 items • Updated about 12 hours ago • 5 System theme Company TOS Privacy About Careers Website Models Datasets Spaces Pricing Docs \n \n \n \n \n \n"
